{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"title":"mergeRemote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence0B11CoordinatorCAA0A00A10ObservableRzrlE11mergeRemote4into3ids7deleted6policyyAD5StoreCyxq_G_Shy10Foundation4UUIDVGAqA11MergePolicyVSgtYaF","extendedModule":"SwiduxPersistence","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mergeRemote","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"into","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC","text":"Store","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ids","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deleted","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"policy","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiduxPersistence11MergePolicyV","text":"MergePolicy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Re-hydration restricted to the rows a caller already knows changed."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistencecoordinator\/mergeremote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeRemote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"kind":"attribute","text":"MainActor","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mergeRemote"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"into"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"store"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Store","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"State"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"ids"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Set","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UUID","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"deleted"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Set","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UUID","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV"},{"kind":"text","text":"> = [], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"policy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MergePolicy","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiduxPersistence11MergePolicyV"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"store","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The live store to reconcile."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"ids","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The identities to re-read. IDs matching no row, and IDs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"belonging to another entity type, are harmless."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"deleted","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Identities known to have been deleted elsewhere."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"policy","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Narrows the configured policy for this call only."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The O(k) counterpart to ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","isActive":true},{"text":", which re-reads every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row of every registered entity on every tick. Where a sync signal carries","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" identities changed, this spends that knowledge: one batched fetch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per 500 IDs instead of a full-table scan, and only the named entities are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reconciled. Everything else in state is left exactly as it was.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every guarantee ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","isActive":true},{"text":" makes holds here. Pending","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes are flushed first; an ID with unflushed local intent — a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drained-but-unflushed write, an un-drained edit, a pending deletion, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"write whose save failed, or an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/editing","isActive":true},{"text":" hold — always wins, and that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not configurable.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A partial read cannot tell a deleted row from one that was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never asked about, so this "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"never"}]},{"type":"text","text":" infers a deletion. An ID vanishes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only if you name it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deleted"},{"type":"text","text":", and only if the resolved policy grants"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/removesMissingEntities","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Name only what you have positive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"evidence for — a history tombstone, not an empty fetch. In exchange,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"there is no empty-snapshot guard to work around: this can remove the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last surviving entity, which "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" cannot."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An ID named in ","type":"text"},{"code":"deleted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that storage ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"still holds"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is not removed. A live","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row is evidence the deletion was itself undone elsewhere; a tombstone can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be stale.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Deferred rows are re-offered","level":2,"anchor":"Deferred-rows-are-re-offered"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tick may read a row and decline to apply it — an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/editing","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" hold is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one exemption that leaves no other trace. Those rows are remembered by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identity and re-offered on the next call, on top of whatever "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ids"},{"type":"text","text":" names,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a caller does not have to re-queue them against its own signal. That"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matters here because a sync signal is generally not resent and releasing a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hold writes no transaction of its own, so without it a hold would quietly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"become a veto. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeChanges(into:policy:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" shares the same debt, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"either path settles what the other deferred. Both discard it when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"container is swapped."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Registered "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse:"},{"type":"text","text":" resolvers do not run here — a resolver is handed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the whole table and asked which rows survive, and a subset would have it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"judge a world it cannot see. Duplicate rows are still collapsed on read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and still reported. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapseDuplicates(into:)-(Store)"},{"type":"text","text":" or a full"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to reclaim them."}]}]}],"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","title":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observation layer."}],"title":"Store","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"title"